       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** the usual limit is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use. Single doses are generally capped at 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove these risks.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum, and is typically used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours.** This is the usual range for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day,** split into 400 mg 4 times daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest a pharmacist or attending review before it's entered. Once you tell me the intended dose, I'll enter it."
      }
